{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) has assigned task #5659: implement `cmd/pr/main.go` for the `pr` utility (paginate or columnate files for printing). The task specifically requires implementing SRD requirements R3.1 (multi-column output), R4.1 (line numbering), R4.2 (indentation and page width), and R4.3 (double-spacing and column separator). The file must compile, pass `go vet`, and satisfy the acceptance criteria from srd110-pr.yaml. This is part of generation run 44 on branch `task/generation-run44-5659`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `pr` utility reimplementation in Go, verified against `gpr` (Homebrew GNU coreutils)\n   - Page layout: 66 lines default (5 header, 56 body, 5 footer), header shows date/filename/page number\n   - Multi-column output: `-COLUMN` or `--columns=COLUMN`, fill-down by default, `-a`/`--across` for fill-across\n   - Line numbering: `-n[CHAR[WIDTH]]` with default separator tab and default width 5\n   - Page indent: `-o MARGIN` adds margin spaces; `-w WIDTH` sets page width (default 72)\n   - Double-spacing: `-d` doubles line spacing; `-s CHAR` sets column separator (default tab)\n   - Page options: `-l N` page length, `-h HEADER` custom header, `-t` omit header/footer, `-T` omit pagination\n   - File input: reads FILE arguments or stdin when no file or \"-\" given\n   - Exit codes: 0 on success, 1 on error\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Non-goal: `-m` (merge files side by side) explicitly excluded\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + SPDX MIT\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines hard limit\n   - File