{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UnBuK35C7MzZKjqkJ4e6te","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G7RS5cvWe3CccJ8cUwz2pj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5659/docs/constitutions/testing.yaml"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":18594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":630,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qo4adosUxbn6s3c33rdpfx","session_id":"b8ba7146-ce80-464f-81bc-b722a4bdfcb1","uuid":"166fa994-06df-446d-8640-f8c83b748b80"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7RS5cvWe3CccJ8cUwz2pj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t#\n4\t# Testing Constitution\n5\t#\n6\t# Rules for test naming, organization, and traceability. Scaffolded into\n7\t# consuming projects so Claude and contributors follow a consistent\n8\t# test structure.\n9\t\n10\tarticles:\n11\t  - id: T1\n12\t    title: Hierarchical test naming\n13\t    rule: |\n14\t      Encode the test suite and use case into every test function name using\n15\t      a fixed prefix: Test{Suite}_UC{NNN}_DescriptiveName.\n16\t\n17\t      {Suite} identifies the test suite (e.g., Rel01, Alpha, Smoke).\n18\t      UC{NNN} is the zero-padded use case number from the spec.\n19\t      DescriptiveName is CamelCase and describes the behavior under test\n20\t      in action-outcome form (e.g., CreateReturnsID, StartFailsWhenLocked).\n21\t\n22\t      The prefix hierarchy enables filtering at any granularity:\n23\t\n24\t        go test -run TestRel01             # entire suite\n25\t        go test -run TestRel01_UC003       # one use case\n26\t        go test -run TestRel01_UC003_Create  # one test\n27\t\n28\t  - id: T2\n29\t    title: One file per use case\n30\t    rule: |\n31\t      Group tests into one file per use case, named uc{NNN}_{slug}_test.go.\n32\t      Shared test infrastructure (setup, helpers, TestMain) lives in a\n33\t      dedicated helpers file (e.g., helpers_test.go). Do not mix tests from\n34\t      different use cases in the same file.\n35\t\n36\t  - id: T3\n37\t    title: Spec-to-code traceability\n38\t    rule: |\n39\t      Every test case entry in the test suite spec must reference the test\n40\t      function that implements it. Every test function must appear in the\n41\t      spec. No orphans in either direction.\n42\t\n43\t      When one test function covers multiple spec entries, each entry\n44\t      references the same function. The entry with the closest name match\n45\t      is the primary; others note the shared coverage.\n46\t\n47\t  - id: T4\n48\t    title: Test count invariant\n49\t    rule: |\n50\t      The number of test functions in a suite must be greater than or equal\n51\t      to the number of test case entries in the corresponding spec. Tests\n52\t      may exceed the spec count (edge cases, performance tests) but must\n53\t      never fall below it. Reorganizing tests must not reduce the total.\n54\t\n55\t  - id: T5\n56\t    title: Mage target naming\n57\t    rule: |\n58\t      Expose each use case as a mage target under the Test namespace:\n59\t\n60\t        (Test) Uc{NNN}{UseCaseSlug}()\n61\t\n62\t      {NNN} is the zero-padded use case number. {UseCaseSlug} is the\n63\t      CamelCase form of the use case slug from the spec (e.g.,\n64\t      OrchestratorInitialization, MeasureWorkflow, BuildTooling).\n65\t\n66\t      Additionally provide test:usecase (all use-case tests), test:unit (package\n67\t      tests), and test:all (both). Examples:\n68\t\n69\t        mage test:uc001OrchestratorInitialization\n70\t        mage test:uc003MeasureWorkflow\n71\t        mage test:usecase\n72\t\n73\tsections:\n74\t  - tag: articles\n75\t    title: Testing Principles\n76\t    content: |\n77\t      Five principles govern the testing phase: hierarchical test naming\n78\t      (Test{Suite}_UC{NNN}_DescriptiveName), one file per use case,\n79\t      bidirectional spec-to-code traceability, a test count invariant that\n80\t      never allows fewer tests than spec entries, and mage test:uc{NNN} targets\n81\t      for each use case.\n82\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qo4adosUxbn6s3c33rdpfx","session_id":"b8ba7146-ce80-464f-81bc-b722a4bdfcb1","uuid":"8614218d-2a44-4388-b35d-4d8ea140e61c","timestamp":"2026-05-29T19:41:12.349Z"}
